    // We need to compute:
    // Total number of valid states: sum over a1 from r to s of C(s - a1 + p - 2, p - 2)
    //   where a1 is Hasan's score, and the remaining p-1 players have sum s - a1, each >= 0
    //   Number of ways to distribute s - a1 among p-1 players = C((s - a1) + (p-1) - 1, (p-1) - 1) = C(s - a1 + p - 2, p - 2)
    //   But we need to be careful: if p-1 == 0, i.e., p == 1, then there's only 1 way if s - a1 == 0, else 0.

