    //     - The remaining p-1-k players have score < x (i.e., <= x-1)
    //     - Sum of all scores = s, so sum of the other p-1 players = s - x
    //     - The k players with score x contribute k*x to the sum
    //     - So the remaining p-1-k players must sum to s - x - k*x = s - (k+1)*x
    //     - Each of these p-1-k players must be in [0, x-1]
    //   Number of such states for fixed x and k:
